* tb_chip_i2c_v10.spice -- auto-generated by script/gen_chip_tb_v10.py
* DO NOT hand-edit -- regenerate instead.
*
* Whole-V10-chip (RING_OSC excluded) I2C WRITE-then-READ testbench at
* SCL=100kHz, using the real TR-1um transistor models and ngspice/
* tr_1um_i2c_slave_async_v10_sim_ready.spice (the LVS-confirmed V10
* chip netlist, M->X + NMOSE->MNE converted -- see script/gen_chip_sim_
* ready_v10.py). Same protocol as V9's own tb_chip_i2c.spice, but V10's
* own pad-pairing-aware terminal reassignment (108.57) means TX_PADS/
* RX_NETS differ from V9's -- see this script's own module docstring.
*
* Protocol:
*   WRITE: S, ADDR+W(0xA0), ACK, DATA=0xA5, ACK, P
*   READ : S, ADDR+R(0xA1), ACK, DATA=0x3C (slave-driven), NACK, P
*
* DIS (P7) held HIGH the whole run (Hi-Z / tx_data-input mode) so the 8
* shared tx/rx pads never contend with this testbench's own TX drive --
* rx_data is instead observed at each pad's own internal receiver net
* (NC_OUT.. ), which reflects the pad regardless of DIS. tx_data is
* held at 0x3C for the whole run (only consumed during the read).

.include '~/Dropbox/91_OpenPDK/TR-1um/libs.tech/spice/models/ip62_models'
.include '../tr_1um_i2c_slave_async_v10_sim_ready.spice'

.param vdd=5.0

vvdd VDD 0 DC 5.0
vvss VSS 0 DC 0

* RSTN: low for 500ns (power-on reset), then a fast edge to VDD,
* held for the rest of the run -- real async reset via each DFFRB's own
* RSTB pin.
vrstn P15 0 PWL(0 0 5e-07 0 6e-07 5.0)

* DIS: held high the whole run (see docstring).
vdis P7 0 DC 5.0

* P9/P10 (RING_OSC.OUTD/OUT in the full chip -- unused and otherwise
* floating here, since RING_OSC is excluded from this netlist). Tied to
* VSS via a large resistor purely for SPICE DC-path/convergence safety.
rp9 P9 VSS 1G
rp10 P10 VSS 1G

* tx_data (bit0..7 = ['P4', 'P12', 'P14', 'P5', 'P6', 'P3', 'P11', 'P13']), held at 0x3C for the whole run.
vtx0 P4 0 DC 0.0
vtx1 P12 0 DC 0.0
vtx2 P14 0 DC 5.0
vtx3 P5 0 DC 5.0
vtx4 P6 0 DC 5.0
vtx5 P3 0 DC 5.0
vtx6 P11 0 DC 0.0
vtx7 P13 0 DC 0.0

* SCL: master clock, 100kHz during bus activity (idle high otherwise).
vscl P1 0 PWL(0 5.000 2e-06 5.000 1.19e-05 5.000 1.2e-05 0.000 1.69e-05 0.000 1.7e-05 5.000 2.19e-05 5.000 2.2e-05 0.000 2.69e-05 0.000 2.7e-05 5.000 3.19e-05 5.000 3.2e-05 0.000 3.69e-05 0.000 3.7e-05 5.000 4.19e-05 5.000 4.2e-05 0.000 4.69e-05 0.000 4.7e-05 5.000 5.19e-05 5.000 5.2e-05 0.000 5.69e-05 0.000 5.7e-05 5.000 6.19e-05 5.000 6.2e-05 0.000 6.69e-05 0.000 6.7e-05 5.000 7.19e-05 5.000 7.2e-05 0.000 7.69e-05 0.000 7.7e-05 5.000 8.19e-05 5.000 8.2e-05 0.000 8.69e-05 0.000 8.7e-05 5.000 9.19e-05 5.000 9.2e-05 0.000 9.69e-05 0.000 9.7e-05 5.000 0.0001019 5.000 0.000102 0.000 0.0001069 0.000 0.000107 5.000 0.0001119 5.000 0.000112 0.000 0.0001169 0.000 0.000117 5.000 0.0001219 5.000 0.000122 0.000 0.0001269 0.000 0.000127 5.000 0.0001319 5.000 0.000132 0.000 0.0001369 0.000 0.000137 5.000 0.0001419 5.000 0.000142 0.000 0.0001469 0.000 0.000147 5.000 0.0001519 5.000 0.000152 0.000 0.0001569 0.000 0.000157 5.000 0.0001619 5.000 0.000162 0.000 0.0001669 0.000 0.000167 5.000 0.0001719 5.000 0.000172 0.000 0.0001769 0.000 0.000177 5.000 0.0001819 5.000 0.000182 0.000 0.0001869 0.000 0.000187 5.000 0.0001919 5.000 0.000192 0.000 0.0001969 0.000 0.000197 5.000 0.000207 5.000 0.000212 5.000 0.0002219 5.000 0.000222 0.000 0.0002269 0.000 0.000227 5.000 0.0002319 5.000 0.000232 0.000 0.0002369 0.000 0.000237 5.000 0.0002419 5.000 0.000242 0.000 0.0002469 0.000 0.000247 5.000 0.0002519 5.000 0.000252 0.000 0.0002569 0.000 0.000257 5.000 0.0002619 5.000 0.000262 0.000 0.0002669 0.000 0.000267 5.000 0.0002719 5.000 0.000272 0.000 0.0002769 0.000 0.000277 5.000 0.0002819 5.000 0.000282 0.000 0.0002869 0.000 0.000287 5.000 0.0002919 5.000 0.000292 0.000 0.0002969 0.000 0.000297 5.000 0.0003019 5.000 0.000302 0.000 0.0003069 0.000 0.000307 5.000 0.0003119 5.000 0.000312 0.000 0.0003169 0.000 0.000317 5.000 0.0003219 5.000 0.000322 0.000 0.0003269 0.000 0.000327 5.000 0.0003319 5.000 0.000332 0.000 0.0003369 0.000 0.000337 5.000 0.0003419 5.000 0.000342 0.000 0.0003469 0.000 0.000347 5.000 0.0003519 5.000 0.000352 0.000 0.0003569 0.000 0.000357 5.000 0.0003619 5.000 0.000362 0.000 0.0003669 0.000 0.000367 5.000 0.0003719 5.000 0.000372 0.000 0.0003769 0.000 0.000377 5.000 0.0003819 5.000 0.000382 0.000 0.0003869 0.000 0.000387 5.000 0.0003919 5.000 0.000392 0.000 0.0003969 0.000 0.000397 5.000 0.0004019 5.000 0.000402 0.000 0.0004069 0.000 0.000407 5.000 0.000417 5.000 0.000422 5.000)

* SDA open-drain bus: this testbench's own master drive (voltage-
* controlled switch to VSS, gated by SDA_CTRL) in parallel with an
* external 10k pull-up to VDD (chip itself has no on-chip SDA
* pull-up) and the DUT's own internal SDA driver (already part of the
* DUT netlist).
vsda_ctrl SDA_CTRL 0 PWL(0 0.000 2e-06 0.000 6.9e-06 0.000 7e-06 5.000 1.22e-05 5.000 1.23e-05 0.000 2.22e-05 0.000 2.23e-05 5.000 3.22e-05 5.000 3.23e-05 0.000 4.22e-05 0.000 4.23e-05 5.000 5.23e-05 5.000 6.23e-05 5.000 7.23e-05 5.000 8.23e-05 5.000 9.22e-05 5.000 9.23e-05 0.000 0.0001023 0.000 0.0001122 0.000 0.0001123 5.000 0.0001222 5.000 0.0001223 0.000 0.0001322 0.000 0.0001323 5.000 0.0001423 5.000 0.0001522 5.000 0.0001523 0.000 0.0001622 0.000 0.0001623 5.000 0.0001722 5.000 0.0001723 0.000 0.0001823 0.000 0.0001922 0.000 0.0001923 5.000 0.0002019 5.000 0.000202 0.000 0.000207 0.000 0.000212 0.000 0.0002169 0.000 0.000217 5.000 0.0002222 5.000 0.0002223 0.000 0.0002322 0.000 0.0002323 5.000 0.0002422 5.000 0.0002423 0.000 0.0002522 0.000 0.0002523 5.000 0.0002623 5.000 0.0002723 5.000 0.0002823 5.000 0.0002922 5.000 0.0002923 0.000 0.0003023 0.000 0.0003123 0.000 0.0003223 0.000 0.0003323 0.000 0.0003423 0.000 0.0003523 0.000 0.0003623 0.000 0.0003723 0.000 0.0003823 0.000 0.0003923 0.000 0.0004022 0.000 0.0004023 5.000 0.0004119 5.000 0.000412 0.000 0.000417 0.000 0.000422 0.000)
.model SDASW SW(RON=10 ROFF=1MEG VT=2.5 VH=0.3)
ssda P2 0 SDA_CTRL 0 SDASW
rpu P2 VDD 10k

* DUT instantiation -- pin order read directly from ngspice/tr_1um_i2c_
* slave_async_v10_sim_ready.spice's own '.subckt tr_1um_i2c_slave_async
* ...' line (not hand-typed), see read_top_pin_order().
xdut P1 P2 P3 P4 P5 P6 P7 VSS P9 P10 P11 P12 P13 P14 P15 VDD tr_1um_i2c_slave_async

.tran 50n 0.000424

* ---- sample points: read-data bits (mid SCL-high window of each of
* the 8 slave-driven bits during the read transaction) ----
.measure tran rd_bit0 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0003195  $ expect ~0V (bit=0)
.measure tran rd_bit1 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0003295  $ expect ~0V (bit=0)
.measure tran rd_bit2 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0003395  $ expect ~VDD (bit=1)
.measure tran rd_bit3 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0003495  $ expect ~VDD (bit=1)
.measure tran rd_bit4 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0003595  $ expect ~VDD (bit=1)
.measure tran rd_bit5 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0003695  $ expect ~VDD (bit=1)
.measure tran rd_bit6 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0003795  $ expect ~0V (bit=0)
.measure tran rd_bit7 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0003895  $ expect ~0V (bit=0)

* ---- ACK sample points (expect ~0V = ACK asserted) ----
.measure tran ack0 FIND v(P2) AT=9.95e-05  $ ACK (slave, address/write)
.measure tran ack1 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0001895  $ ACK (slave, data)
.measure tran ack2 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0003095  $ ACK (slave, address/read)
.measure tran ack3 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0003995  $ NACK (master, ends read)

* ---- diagnostic: internal core state (busy/addr_match/rw), to
* localize a non-responsive-bus result ----
.measure tran busy_after_start FIND v(xdut.NC_CORE_busy) AT=9.5e-06  $ expect ~VDD (busy asserted shortly after START)
.measure tran addr_match_write FIND v(xdut.NC_CORE_addr_match) AT=0.0001018  $ expect ~VDD if address 0x50 matched (ACK (slave, address/write))
.measure tran rw_write FIND v(xdut.NC_CORE_rw) AT=0.0001018  $ expect ~0V (write)
.measure tran addr_match_write_x1 WHEN v(xdut.NC_CORE_addr_match)=2.5 RISE=1  $ addr_match rise #1 (ACK (slave, address/write))
.measure tran addr_match_read FIND v(xdut.NC_CORE_addr_match) AT=0.0003118  $ expect ~VDD if address 0x50 matched (ACK (slave, address/read))
.measure tran rw_read FIND v(xdut.NC_CORE_rw) AT=0.0003118  $ expect ~VDD (read)
.measure tran addr_match_read_x1 WHEN v(xdut.NC_CORE_addr_match)=2.5 RISE=2  $ addr_match rise #2 (ACK (slave, address/read))

* ---- diagnostic: this generator's OWN driven bus level self-check
* (independent of the DUT) for every master-driven address/data bit ----
.measure tran tx_ADDR_W_bit7 FIND v(P2) AT=1.95e-05  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, ADDR+W bit7 (expect ~VDD (bit=1))
.measure tran tx_ADDR_W_bit6 FIND v(P2) AT=2.95e-05  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, ADDR+W bit6 (expect ~0V (bit=0))
.measure tran tx_ADDR_W_bit5 FIND v(P2) AT=3.95e-05  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, ADDR+W bit5 (expect ~VDD (bit=1))
.measure tran tx_ADDR_W_bit4 FIND v(P2) AT=4.95e-05  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, ADDR+W bit4 (expect ~0V (bit=0))
.measure tran tx_ADDR_W_bit3 FIND v(P2) AT=5.95e-05  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, ADDR+W bit3 (expect ~0V (bit=0))
.measure tran tx_ADDR_W_bit2 FIND v(P2) AT=6.95e-05  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, ADDR+W bit2 (expect ~0V (bit=0))
.measure tran tx_ADDR_W_bit1 FIND v(P2) AT=7.95e-05  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, ADDR+W bit1 (expect ~0V (bit=0))
.measure tran tx_ADDR_W_bit0 FIND v(P2) AT=8.95e-05  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, ADDR+W bit0 (expect ~0V (bit=0))
.measure tran tx_DATA_write_bit7 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0001095  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, DATA (write) bit7 (expect ~VDD (bit=1))
.measure tran tx_DATA_write_bit6 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0001195  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, DATA (write) bit6 (expect ~0V (bit=0))
.measure tran tx_DATA_write_bit5 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0001295  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, DATA (write) bit5 (expect ~VDD (bit=1))
.measure tran tx_DATA_write_bit4 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0001395  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, DATA (write) bit4 (expect ~0V (bit=0))
.measure tran tx_DATA_write_bit3 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0001495  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, DATA (write) bit3 (expect ~0V (bit=0))
.measure tran tx_DATA_write_bit2 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0001595  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, DATA (write) bit2 (expect ~VDD (bit=1))
.measure tran tx_DATA_write_bit1 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0001695  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, DATA (write) bit1 (expect ~0V (bit=0))
.measure tran tx_DATA_write_bit0 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0001795  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, DATA (write) bit0 (expect ~VDD (bit=1))
.measure tran tx_ADDR_R_bit7 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0002295  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, ADDR+R bit7 (expect ~VDD (bit=1))
.measure tran tx_ADDR_R_bit6 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0002395  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, ADDR+R bit6 (expect ~0V (bit=0))
.measure tran tx_ADDR_R_bit5 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0002495  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, ADDR+R bit5 (expect ~VDD (bit=1))
.measure tran tx_ADDR_R_bit4 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0002595  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, ADDR+R bit4 (expect ~0V (bit=0))
.measure tran tx_ADDR_R_bit3 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0002695  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, ADDR+R bit3 (expect ~0V (bit=0))
.measure tran tx_ADDR_R_bit2 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0002795  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, ADDR+R bit2 (expect ~0V (bit=0))
.measure tran tx_ADDR_R_bit1 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0002895  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, ADDR+R bit1 (expect ~0V (bit=0))
.measure tran tx_ADDR_R_bit0 FIND v(P2) AT=0.0002995  $ self-check: this generator's OWN driven bus level, ADDR+R bit0 (expect ~VDD (bit=1))

* ---- diagnostic: internal address shift-register (shreg_0..shreg_6,
* inside xdut.x2 = i2c_slave_async_nrow_fm) snapshot right after each
* address byte's last-bit SCL edge ----
.measure tran shreg_0_write FIND v(xdut.x2.shreg_0) AT=8.9e-05  $ internal address shift-reg bit, right after the ADDR+W last-bit SCL edge
.measure tran shreg_1_write FIND v(xdut.x2.shreg_1) AT=8.9e-05  $ internal address shift-reg bit, right after the ADDR+W last-bit SCL edge
.measure tran shreg_2_write FIND v(xdut.x2.shreg_2) AT=8.9e-05  $ internal address shift-reg bit, right after the ADDR+W last-bit SCL edge
